## Section A -- What Stage 21 may consume from Stage 20

Stage 21 may read the following Stage 20.2 / Stage 20.3 artifacts
as deterministic, lineage-validated inputs:

- Stage 20.2: manifest.json, preview_candidates.csv,
  alert_eligibility_decisions.csv, README.md, stage20_run.log
- Stage 20.3: stage20_3_manifest.json,
  filter_interface_registry.csv, filter_interface_results.csv,
  README.md, stage20_3_run.log

The closure attestation in stage20_closure_manifest.json pins
each artifact's SHA-256 at the moment of closure. Stage 21 must
not mutate any of these files.

## Section B -- What Stage 21 must build fresh

Stage 21 introduces the first real private-preview ping path.
It must build its own:

- Provider clients (if any).
- Renderer / formatter for the preview message.
- Routing decision logic (which channel each preview goes to).
- Dispatch sink (Discord webhook, Telegram bot, etc.), bound to
  operator-controlled private channels only.

Stage 21 must NOT re-derive Stage 20.2 / Stage 20.3 outputs at
runtime; it consumes them as immutable inputs.

## Section C -- Private preview boundary

All Stage 21 outputs route to private operator-controlled channel(s)
only. No subscriber routing, no public channel routing, no paid-signal
routing.

Every Stage 21 preview ping must carry an explicit, visible dry-run /
private-preview marker that makes the message's non-actionable status
unambiguous to the reader. The exact rendered phrasing is a Stage 21
decision and should align with prior PHX2 internal-preview conventions
(see Stage 8C if applicable). Stage 20.4 does not lock the exact text.

The marker requirement is non-negotiable. The exact text is a Stage 21
design call.

## Section D -- Hard rules Stage 21 inherits

Phoenix1 isolation (locked).

Stage 21 must not import Phoenix1 code, and must not depend on Phoenix1
runtime state as its live provider path. Any Phoenix1 comparison/replay
must remain offline and separately scoped (see Stage 16 for the
replay/comparison stage, when implemented).

Concretely:
- No `import phoenix1` or any submodule thereof in Stage 21 modules.
- No reads from a live Phoenix1 database connection in Stage 21 runtime.
- Phoenix1 may only be used by separately-scoped offline tools
  (Stage 16 replay/comparator), running outside the Stage 21 live
  preview pipeline.

