This is a baseline snapshot, not an authoritative count. Stage 21
must run the full Stage 20 suite itself and verify a clean green
before its own work proceeds.

## Section F -- Stage 21 must explicitly define separately

The following surfaces are NOT inherited from Stage 20.4 and must
be designed and locked separately in Stage 21:

- Real (non-empty) filter implementations.
- Threshold tuning per filter mode.
- Live dispatch authorization gates. The closure manifest pins
  live_dispatch_ready to the literal Python False. Stage 21 must
  define how and when that gate flips.
- Operator-facing dashboard or observability surface.

## Section G -- Forbidden in Stage 21 v0

- Any safety-flag flip to a true value in source. The closure
  auditor will reject any such hit on the next closure run.
- Network calls outside operator-controlled private channels.
- Phoenix1 imports (see Section D).
- Reading any environment variable that contains an API key or
  webhook URL into the live preview path. Load such values via
  a separately scoped, attestable mechanism instead.

